61905 230,-6019.627058970831 230.5,-6166.247758465674 231,-6316.283692782036 231.5,-6469.814412958266 232,-6626.921323014419 232.5,-6787.687723113777 233,-6952.198853729639 233.5,-7120.541940841036 234,-7292.8062421810355 234.5,-7469.083094562414 235,-7649.465962305571 235.5,-7834.050486794649 236,-8022.934537187799 236.50000000000003,-8216.21826230873 237,-8414.00414374688 237.5,-8616.397050194613 238,-8823.504293049913 238.49999999999997,-9035.435683314328 239,-9252.303589816242 239.5,-9474.222998790228 240,-9701.311574844394 240.5,-9933.689723347637 241,-10171.480654270203 241.5,-10414.810447511163 242,-10663.808119747759 242.5,-10918.60569284169 243,-11179.338263838874 243.5,-11446.144076599612 244,-11719.164595097449 244.5,-11998.544578425142 245,-12284.432157547912 245.5,-12576.978913844323 246,-12876.339959476909 246.5,-13182.674019634569 247,-13496.143516690845 247.5,-13816.914656322275 248,-14145.157515633027 248.5,-14481.046133331922 249.00000000000003,-14824.758602010095 249.5,-15176.47716256796 250,-15536.388300841898 250.5,-15904.682846481404 250.99999999999997,-16281.556074129538 251.5,-16667.207806960138 252,-17061.842522626583 252.5,-17465.669461678764 253,-17878.90273850505 253.5,-18301.76145485864 254,-18734.469816028064 254.5,-19177.257249714025 254.99999999999997,-19630.358527674845 255.50000000000003,-20094.01389020565 256,-20568.469173516776 256.5,-21053.97594007963 257,-21550.79161200828 257.5,-22059.179607548172 258,-22579.40948074376 258.5,-23111.757064359907 259,-23656.5046161319 259.5,-24213.940968422332 260,-24784.36168136362 260.5,-25368.069199568243 261,-25965.373012488613 261.5,-26576.58981851266 262,-27202.043692881238 262.5,-27842.06625951745 263,-28496.99686685783 263.5,-29167.182767779417 264,-29852.979303717904 264.5,-30554.750093074108 265,-31272.86722400965 265.5,-32007.711451732746 266,-32759.672400379823 266.5,-33529.148769599095 267,-34316.54854594681 267.5,-35122.28921920687 268,-35946.79800374953 268.5,-36790.512065045885 269,-37653.878751459175 269.5,-38537.35583143456 270,-39441.41173621411 270.5,-40366.52580820498 271,-41313.18855513354 271.5,-42281.901910118795 272,-43273.17949780407 272.5,-44287.54690668729 273,-45325.541967795485 273.5,-46387.71503984952 274,-47474.629301071844 274.5,-48586.86104779056 275,-49725\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"red\" stroke-width=\"1\"></polyline><foreignObject x=\"115\" y=\"10\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" style=\"color: red;\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math></div></foreignObject></svg><figcaption>Graphs of some exponential functions <math><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow></math>.</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"The graphs of some typical exponential functions are shown in the previous figure. They all pass through the point ``\\left(0,1\\right)`` since ``a^0=1`` for every ``a>0``. Observe that ``a^x>0`` for all ``a>0`` and all real ``x`` and that:\n\n- If ``a>1``, then ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty}a^x = 0`` and ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}a^x = \\infty``.\n- If ``0<a<1``, then ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty}a^x = \\infty`` and ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}a^x = 0``.","output":"","result":"The graphs of some typical exponential functions are shown in the previous figure. They all pass through the point ``\\left(0,1\\right)`` since ``a^0=1`` for every ``a>0``. Observe that ``a^x>0`` for all ``a>0`` and all real ``x`` and that:\n\n- If ``a>1``, then ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty}a^x = 0`` and ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}a^x = \\infty``.\n- If ``0<a<1``, then ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty}a^x = \\infty`` and ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}a^x = 0``.","resultHTML":"<p>The graphs of some typical exponential functions are shown in the previous figure. They all pass through the point <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\left(0,1\\right)\\)</span> since <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a^0=1\\)</span> for every <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a&gt;0\\)</span>. Observe that <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a^x&gt;0\\)</span> for all <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a&gt;0\\)</span> and all real <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(x\\)</span> and that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a&gt;1\\)</span>, then <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty}a^x = 0\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}a^x = \\infty\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>If <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(0&lt;a&lt;1\\)</span>, then <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -\\infty}a^x = \\infty\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}a^x = 0\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"### Logarithms\n\nThe function ``f\\left(x\\right)=a^x`` is a bijective function provided that ``a>0`` and ``a\\ne1``. Therefore, ``f`` has an inverse which we call a *logarithmic function*.\n\n::: definition\nIf ``a>0`` and ``a\\ne 1``, the function ``\\log_ax``,  called the logarithm of ``x`` to the base ``a``, is the inverse of the bijective function ``a^x``:\n```math\n\\forall a>0,a\\ne1:x=a^y\\implies y=\\log_ax\\,.\n```\n:::\n\nSince ``a^x`` has domain ``\\left]-\\infty,\\infty\\right[``, ``\\log_a x`` has range ``\\left]-\\infty,\\infty\\right[``. Since ``a^x`` has range ``\\left]0,\\infty\\right[``, ``\\log_a x`` has domain ``\\left]0,\\infty\\right[``. Since ``a^x`` and ``\\log_a x`` are inverse functions, the following cancellation identities hold:\n```math\n\\log_a\\left(a^x\\right)=x\\textrm{ for all real }x\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad a^{\\log_a x}=x\\textrm{ for all }x>0\\,.\n```","output":"","result":"### Logarithms\n\nThe function ``f\\left(x\\right)=a^x`` is a bijective function provided that ``a>0`` and ``a\\ne1``. Therefore, ``f`` has an inverse which we call a *logarithmic function*.\n\n::: definition\nIf ``a>0`` and ``a\\ne 1``, the function ``\\log_ax``,  called the logarithm of ``x`` to the base ``a``, is the inverse of the bijective function ``a^x``:\n```math\n\\forall a>0,a\\ne1:x=a^y\\implies y=\\log_ax\\,.\n```\n:::\n\nSince ``a^x`` has domain ``\\left]-\\infty,\\infty\\right[``, ``\\log_a x`` has range ``\\left]-\\infty,\\infty\\right[``. Since ``a^x`` has range ``\\left]0,\\infty\\right[``, ``\\log_a x`` has domain ``\\left]0,\\infty\\right[``. Since ``a^x`` and ``\\log_a x`` are inverse functions, the following cancellation identities hold:\n```math\n\\log_a\\left(a^x\\right)=x\\textrm{ for all real }x\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad a^{\\log_a x}=x\\textrm{ for all }x>0\\,.\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-ES111_051Lecture05-c3637-logarithms\">\n<h1>Logarithms</h1>\n<p>The function <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f\\left(x\\right)=a^x\\)</span> is a bijective function provided that <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a&gt;0\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a\\ne1\\)</span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f\\)</span> has an inverse which we call a <em>logarithmic function</em>.</p>\n<div data-type=\"definition\">\n<p>If <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a&gt;0\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a\\ne 1\\)</span>, the function <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\log_ax\\)</span>,  called the logarithm of <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(x\\)</span> to the base <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a\\)</span>, is the inverse of the bijective function <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a^x\\)</span>:</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\forall a&gt;0,a\\ne1:x=a^y\\implies y=\\log_ax\\,.\n\\]\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Since <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a^x\\)</span> has domain <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\left]-\\infty,\\infty\\right[\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\log_a x\\)</span> has range <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\left]-\\infty,\\infty\\right[\\)</span>. Since <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a^x\\)</span> has range <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\left]0,\\infty\\right[\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\log_a x\\)</span> has domain <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\left]0,\\infty\\right[\\)</span>. Since <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(a^x\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\log_a x\\)</span> are inverse functions, the following cancellation identities hold:</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\log_a\\left(a^x\\right)=x\\textrm{ for all real }x\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad a^{\\log_a x}=x\\textrm{ for all }x&gt;0\\,.\n\\]\n</div>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 50;\nconst fontX = 14;\nconst fontY = 18;\nconst xmid = 0.5 * scale;\nconst ymid = 2.5 * scale;\n\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n    width: 6 * scale,\n    height: 5 * scale,\n    caption: String.raw`Graphs of some logarithmic functions \\(y=\\log_a x\\).`,\n});\n\nfigure.axes({\n    origin: [xmid, ymid],\n    scale,\n    x: { ticks: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] },\n    y: { ticks: [-2, -1, 1, 2] },\n});\n\nconst curves = [\n    [0.1, \"cyan\", String.raw`a=\\frac{1}{10}`, 2.75, 2],\n    [0.25, \"RoyalBlue\", String.raw`a=\\frac{1}{4}`, 3.25, 2],\n    [0.5, \"purple\", String.raw`a=\\frac{1}{2}`, 4.4, 2],\n    [2, \"green\", \"a=2\", 0.2, 1],\n    [4, \"orange\", \"a=4\", 1.3, 1],\n    [10, \"red\", \"a=10\", 1.8, 1],\n];\n\nfor (const [a, color, tex, y, rows] of curves) {\n    figure.plot((x) => Math.log(x) / Math.log(a), {\n        domain: [0.01, 5.5],\n        samples: 550,\n        width: 1,\n        stroke: color,\n    });\n\n    const label = figure.math()\n        .x(5 * scale)\n        .y(y * scale)\n        .width(4 * fontX)\n        .height(rows * fontY)\n        .latex(tex);\n\n    label.element().style.color = color;\n}\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"xy12345−2−112a=110a=14a=12a=2a=4a=10Graphs of some logarithmic functions y=loga⁡x.","resultHTML":"<figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"300\" height=\"250\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 250\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><line x1=\"25\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"25\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><polygon points=\"300,125 293,121 293,129\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><polygon points=\"25,0 21,7 29,7\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"286\" y=\"95\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"33\" y=\"-2\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"121\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"129\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"59\" y=\"133\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" style=\"display: flex; width: 100%; height: 100%; justify-content: center; align-items: flex-start;\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"121\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"129\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"109\" y=\"133\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" style=\"display: flex; width: 100%; height: 100%; justify-content: center; align-items: flex-start;\"><math><mn>2</mn></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"175\" y1=\"121\" x2=\"175\" y2=\"129\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"159\" y=\"133\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=