0309286568573 187.6,61.45668270417195 188,61.11027254265817 188.4,60.763862381144406 188.8,60.417452219630626 189.2,60.07104205811685 189.6,59.72463189660307 190,59.3782217350893 190.4,59.03181157357552 190.8,58.68540141206175 191.2,58.33899125054798 191.6,57.992581089034196 192,57.646170927520416 192.4,57.29976076600664 192.8,56.95335060449287 193.2,56.60694044297909 193.60000000000002,56.26053028146532 194,55.91412011995155 194.4,55.56770995843776 194.8,55.22129979692399 195.2,54.87488963541023 195.6,54.52847947389644 196,54.182069312382666 196.39999999999998,53.83565915086889 196.8,53.48924898935512 197.2,53.142838827841345 197.6,52.79642866632757 198,52.450018504813784 198.4,52.10360834330001 198.8,51.75719818178624 199.2,51.41078802027246 199.6,51.06437785875869 200,50.717967697244916\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"RoyalBlue\" stroke-width=\"1\"></polyline><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"50.717967697244916\" r=\"3\" fill=\"RoyalBlue\" stroke=\"RoyalBlue\"></circle></svg><figcaption>The shaded area is <math><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> square units.</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"Observe that, similar to the corresponding values of ``\\cos x`` and ``\\sin x``, we have\n```math\n\\cosh 0 = 1\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\sinh 0 = 0\\,,\n```\nand ``\\cosh x``, like ``\\cos x``, is an even function, and ``\\sinh x``, like ``\\sin x``, is an odd function:\n```math\n\\cosh\\left(-x\\right)=\\cosh x\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\sinh\\left(-x\\right)=-\\sinh x\\,.\n```\n\nThe graph ``y=\\cosh x`` is called a *catenary*. A chain hanging by its ends will assume the shape of a catenary.","output":"","result":"Observe that, similar to the corresponding values of ``\\cos x`` and ``\\sin x``, we have\n```math\n\\cosh 0 = 1\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\sinh 0 = 0\\,,\n```\nand ``\\cosh x``, like ``\\cos x``, is an even function, and ``\\sinh x``, like ``\\sin x``, is an odd function:\n```math\n\\cosh\\left(-x\\right)=\\cosh x\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\sinh\\left(-x\\right)=-\\sinh x\\,.\n```\n\nThe graph ``y=\\cosh x`` is called a *catenary*. A chain hanging by its ends will assume the shape of a catenary.","resultHTML":"<p>Observe that, similar to the corresponding values of <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\cos x\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\sin x\\)</span>, we have</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\cosh 0 = 1\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\sinh 0 = 0\\,,\n\\]\n</div>\n<p>and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\cosh x\\)</span>, like <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\cos x\\)</span>, is an even function, and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\sinh x\\)</span>, like <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\sin x\\)</span>, is an odd function:</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\cosh\\left(-x\\right)=\\cosh x\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\sinh\\left(-x\\right)=-\\sinh x\\,.\n\\]\n</div>\n<p>The graph <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(y=\\cosh x\\)</span> is called a <em>catenary</em>. A chain hanging by its ends will assume the shape of a catenary.</p>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 40;\n\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n    width: 6 * scale,\n    height: 6 * scale,\n    caption: String.raw`The graphs of \\(\\cosh x\\) (red) and \\(\\sinh x\\) (blue).`,\n});\n\nfigure.axes({\n    origin: [3 * scale, 3 * scale],\n    scale,\n    x: { ticks: [] },\n    y: { ticks: [1] },\n});\n\nfigure.plot(Math.cosh, {\n    domain: [-3, 3],\n    samples: 601,\n    width: 1,\n    stroke: \"red\",\n});\n\nfigure.plot(Math.sinh, {\n    domain: [-3, 3],\n    samples: 601,\n    width: 1,\n    stroke: \"RoyalBlue\",\n});\n\nfigure.point(2, Math.sinh(2), {\n    radius: 3,\n    fill: \"RoyalBlue\",\n    stroke: \"RoyalBlue\",\n});\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"xy1The graphs of cosh⁡x (red) and sinh⁡x (blue).","resultHTML":"<figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"240\" height=\"240\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 240\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><polygon points=\"240,120 233,116 233,124\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><polygon points=\"120,0 116,7 124,7\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"226\" y=\"90\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"128\" y=\"-2\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"116\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"80\" y=\"64\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" style=\"display: flex; width: 100%; height: 100%; justify-content: flex-end; align-items: center;\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></div></foreignObject><polyline points=\"0,-282.70647983111064 0.3999999999999915,-278.7193985657665 0.7999999999999972,-274.772189572546 1.1999999999999886,-270.8644581272608 1.5999999999999943,-266.99581345350964 2,-263.1658686836017 2.4000000000000057,-259.37424081986774 2.799999999999997,-255.62055069636233 3.200000000000003,-251.90442294094453 3.5999999999999943,-248.2254859377423 4,-244.58337178998937 4.3999999999999915,-240.97771628323608 4.800000000000011,-237.40815884892663 5.199999999999989,-233.8743425283434 5.6000000000000085,-230.37591393690917 6,-226.91252322884958 6.400000000000006,-223.48382406220753 6.799999999999997,-220.08947356420936 7.200000000000003,-216.72913229697622 7.599999999999994,-213.4024642235815 8,-210.10913667444532 8.400000000000006,-206.84882031406858 8.800000000000011,-203.62118910809806 9.200000000000003,-200.42592029072364 9.600000000000009,-197.2626943324007 10,-194.13119490789757 10.399999999999991,-191.0311088646621 