065 218.79999999999998,-114.75723985289588 219.20000000000002,-117.15042384513825 219.60000000000002,-119.56732307739094 220,-122.0081792415915 220.39999999999998,-124.47323642539035 220.79999999999998,-126.96274113656014 221.20000000000002,-129.47694232764673 221.6,-132.01609142086403 222,-134.5804423332375 222.39999999999998,-137.17025150199544 222.8,-139.78577791021303 223.2,-142.42728311271026 223.6,-145.09503126220886 224,-147.78928913574708 224.4,-150.51032616135745 224.8,-153.2584144450098 225.2,-156.03382879782276 225.6,-158.83684676354443 226,-161.6677486463076 226.4,-164.52681753865897 226.8,-167.41433934987072 227.2,-170.33060283453017 227.60000000000002,-173.27589962141633 228,-176.25052424266175 228.4,-179.25477416320768 228.79999999999998,-182.28894981054975 229.20000000000002,-185.35335460478154 229.60000000000002,-188.4482949889354 230,-191.57408045962927 230.39999999999998,-194.7310235980151 230.79999999999998,-197.91944010103737 231.20000000000002,-201.13964881300382 231.6,-204.39197175746858 232,-207.6767341694366 232.39999999999998,-210.9942645278864 232.8,-214.34489458861879 233.2,-217.72895941743138 233.6,-221.1467974236275 234,-224.59875039385588 234.4,-228.08516352629056 234.8,-231.60638546514946 235.2,-235.16276833556128 235.6,-238.75466777877648 236,-242.38244298773316 236.4,-246.04645674297473 236.8,-249.74707544893022 237.2,-253.4846691705543 237.60000000000002,-257.259611670334 238,-261.0722804456643 238.4,-264.92305676660067 238.79999999999998,-268.81232571398385 239.20000000000002,-272.7404762179501 239.60000000000002,-276.70790109682275 240,-280.71499709639613\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"RoyalBlue\" stroke-width=\"1\"></polyline><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"-25.07441631388076\" r=\"3\" fill=\"RoyalBlue\" stroke=\"RoyalBlue\"></circle></svg><figcaption>The graphs of <math><mrow><mrow><mi>cosh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> (red) and <math><mrow><mrow><mi>sinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace></mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> (blue).</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"Many other properties of the hyperbolic functions resemble those of the corresponding circular functions, sometimes with signs changed.\n\n!!! example \"Show that\"\n\n\t```math\n\t\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\cosh x=\\sinh x\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\sinh x=\\cosh x\n\t```\n\n\tWe have\n\n\t```math\n\t\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\cosh x=\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x+\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}{2}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x+\\mathcal{e}^{-x}\\left(-1\\right)}{2}=\\sinh x\n\t```\n\t\n\t```math\n\t\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\sinh x=\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x-\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}{2}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x-\\mathcal{e}^{-x}\\left(-1\\right)}{2}=\\cosh x\\,.\n\t```\n\nThe following addition formulas and double-angle formulas can be checked algebraically by using the definition of ``\\mathrm{cosh}`` and ``\\mathrm{sinh}`` and the laws of exponents:\n```math\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cosh\\left(x+y\\right)&=\\cosh x\\cosh y+\\sinh x\\sinh y\\,,\\\\\n\\sinh\\left(x+y\\right)&=\\sinh x\\cosh y+\\cosh x\\sinh y\\,,\\\\\n\\cosh\\left(2x\\right)&=\\cosh^2x+\\sinh^2x=1+2\\sinh^2x=2\\cosh^2x-1\\,,\\\\\n\\sinh\\left(2x\\right)&=2\\sinh x\\cosh x\\,.\n\\end{aligned}\n```\n\nBy analogy with the trigonometric functions, other hyperbolic functions can be defined in terms of ``\\mathrm{cosh}`` and ``\\mathrm{sinh}``.\n\n::: definition\n```math\n\\tanh x=\\frac{\\sinh x}{\\cosh x}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x-\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}{\\mathcal{e}^x+\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}=\\frac{1-\\mathcal{e}^{-2x}}{1+\\mathcal{e}^{-2x}}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^{2x}-1}{\\mathcal{e}^{2x}+1}\\,.\n```\n:::\n","output":"","result":"Many other properties of the hyperbolic functions resemble those of the corresponding circular functions, sometimes with signs changed.\n\n!!! example \"Show that\"\n\n\t```math\n\t\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\cosh x=\\sinh x\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\sinh x=\\cosh x\n\t```\n\n\tWe have\n\n\t```math\n\t\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\cosh x=\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x+\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}{2}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x+\\mathcal{e}^{-x}\\left(-1\\right)}{2}=\\sinh x\n\t```\n\t\n\t```math\n\t\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\sinh x=\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x-\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}{2}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x-\\mathcal{e}^{-x}\\left(-1\\right)}{2}=\\cosh x\\,.\n\t```\n\nThe following addition formulas and double-angle formulas can be checked algebraically by using the definition of ``\\mathrm{cosh}`` and ``\\mathrm{sinh}`` and the laws of exponents:\n```math\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cosh\\left(x+y\\right)&=\\cosh x\\cosh y+\\sinh x\\sinh y\\,,\\\\\n\\sinh\\left(x+y\\right)&=\\sinh x\\cosh y+\\cosh x\\sinh y\\,,\\\\\n\\cosh\\left(2x\\right)&=\\cosh^2x+\\sinh^2x=1+2\\sinh^2x=2\\cosh^2x-1\\,,\\\\\n\\sinh\\left(2x\\right)&=2\\sinh x\\cosh x\\,.\n\\end{aligned}\n```\n\nBy analogy with the trigonometric functions, other hyperbolic functions can be defined in terms of ``\\mathrm{cosh}`` and ``\\mathrm{sinh}``.\n\n::: definition\n```math\n\\tanh x=\\frac{\\sinh x}{\\cosh x}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x-\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}{\\mathcal{e}^x+\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}=\\frac{1-\\mathcal{e}^{-2x}}{1+\\mathcal{e}^{-2x}}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^{2x}-1}{\\mathcal{e}^{2x}+1}\\,.\n```\n:::\n","resultHTML":"<p>Many other properties of the hyperbolic functions resemble those of the corresponding circular functions, sometimes with signs changed.</p>\n<aside data-type=\"example\">\n<h5>Show that</h5>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\cosh x=\\sinh x\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\sinh x=\\cosh x\n\\]\n</div>\n<p>We have</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\cosh x=\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x+\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}{2}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x+\\mathcal{e}^{-x}\\left(-1\\right)}{2}=\\sinh x\n\\]\n</div>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\sinh x=\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\hphantom{x}}{\\mathrm{d} x}\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x-\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}{2}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x-\\mathcal{e}^{-x}\\left(-1\\right)}{2}=\\cosh x\\,.\n\\]\n</div>\n</aside>\n<p>The following addition formulas and double-angle formulas can be checked algebraically by using the definition of <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\mathrm{cosh}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\mathrm{sinh}\\)</span> and the laws of exponents:</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cosh\\left(x+y\\right)&amp;=\\cosh x\\cosh y+\\sinh x\\sinh y\\,,\\\\\n\\sinh\\left(x+y\\right)&amp;=\\sinh x\\cosh y+\\cosh x\\sinh y\\,,\\\\\n\\cosh\\left(2x\\right)&amp;=\\cosh^2x+\\sinh^2x=1+2\\sinh^2x=2\\cosh^2x-1\\,,\\\\\n\\sinh\\left(2x\\right)&amp;=2\\sinh x\\cosh x\\,.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n</div>\n<p>By analogy with the trigonometric functions, other hyperbolic functions can be defined in terms of <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\mathrm{cosh}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\mathrm{sinh}\\)</span>.</p>\n<div data-type=\"definition\">\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\tanh x=\\frac{\\sinh x}{\\cosh x}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^x-\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}{\\mathcal{e}^x+\\mathcal{e}^{-x}}=\\frac{1-\\mathcal{e}^{-2x}}{1+\\mathcal{e}^{-2x}}=\\frac{\\mathcal{e}^{2x}-1}{\\mathcal{e}^{2x}+1}\\,.\n\\]\n</div>\n</div>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 40;\n\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n    width: 12 * scale,\n    height: 3 * scale,\n    caption: String.raw`The graphs of \\(\\tanh x\\).`,\n    wide: true,\n});\n\nfigure.axes({\n    origin: [6 * scale, 1.5 * scale],\n    scale,\n    x: { ticks: [] },\n    y: { ticks: [-1, 1] },\n});\n\nfigure.plot(Math.tanh, {\n    domain: [-6, 6],\n    samples: 1201,\n    width: 1,\n    stroke: \"red\",\n});\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"xy−11The graphs of tanh⁡x.","resultHTML":"<figure class=\"wide\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"480\" height=\"120\" viewBox=\"0 0 480 120\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><polygon points=\"480,60 473,56 473,64\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><polygon points=\"240,0 236,7 244,7\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"466\" y=\"30\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"248\" y=\"-2\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"236\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"244\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"200\" y=\"84\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" style=\"display: flex; width: 100%; height: 100%; justify-content: flex-end; align-items: center;\"><math><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"236\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"244\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"200\" y=\"4\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" style=\"display: flex; width: 100%; height: 100%; justify-content: flex-end; align-items: center;\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></div></foreignObject><polyline points=\"0,99.99950846603183 0.39999999999997726,99.9994